+# System startup correspondence and remaining stage3 scope — 2026-11-12
+
+## Authority and bounded result
+
+This is pseudocode → sourcecode translation, not product/API design. Source45 > PlusCal25 > code139/stale; policy, upper meaning and lineage are unchanged. `sourcescript/system.py:208-237` and the complete `pseudocode/system.pcal:14-49` specify initial candidate validation, prerequisite checking, supplied initial rendering, ready, API exposure, Mantine mount and final invariant audit. The actual system caller previously exposed the public API before rendering/ready, omitted a prerequisite gate and audited before mount. Earlier stage1 supplied-renderer closure did not establish this complete system-caller order. This correction qualifies that historical closure: renderer procedure coverage remains, but system orchestration needed the changes recorded here. It is not a reason to rewrite already-translated procedures for volume.
+
+## Procedure / branch / real-caller map
+
+| Authoritative step | Target translation and actual call path |
+| --- | --- |
+| `CreateValidatedInitialProject` | `sourcecode/system.js:initializeFastFigure()` invokes Backend `initializeActiveProject()`. `sourcecode/backend/project_state.js:initializeActiveProject()` now creates the candidate, calls `validateProjectObjectState(candidate,{requireSlots:true})`, then binds the new `ProjectObject`. Failure leaves the previous binding untouched; no empty initial authority is published first. Existing constructor validation is retained, not a new validation protocol. No CSV or fake chart is created. |
+| `RequireCoreAndHosts` | After concrete registry/FSM construction, `requireCoreRuntimeAndRendererHosts()` checks existing required callable/type bindings and the required renderer host IDs, Plotly presentation function and UI runtime/root. Missing prerequisites throw before supplied presentation, ready, public publication or mount. These concrete platform checks realize the specified assertion; no new recover/retry/fallback/lifecycle branch. |
+| Concrete lexical bindings | Existing `REQUIRED_APP_FUNCTIONS` incorrectly tested absent `importProject`/`makeSlots` identifiers. It now imports/tests the actual project import wrapper `importProjectFile` and initial candidate owner `createProjectState`. Other audit checks remain. The shared required-host list is reused by the startup guard and existing manual/final audit, not duplicated as project state. |
+| `PrepareBoundaryInputs` / `PrepareAndRenderCore` | Existing Application `startupCoreRuntime()` obtains the one official renderer projection and Interface read, builds public action references from real wrappers, then calls `startupCoreRuntimeProjection`. That frontend procedure preserves zoom → controller → existing slots → style → supplied-reference audit. It does not depend on early `window.FastFigureApi` publication. Physical placement of those Application-owned steps is retained; no second read/store/authority. |
+| `ReadyThroughApplication` | Existing Application facade `appFSM.ready()` remains after supplied rendering, using owner-resolved workspace. This change does not manufacture a second lifecycle state or event. |
+| `ExposeExistingBoundary` | `publishPublicApi()` is moved after ready. Its existing immutable public composition and individual public outputs are unchanged. |
+| `MountExistingUi` / `AuditStartup` | Existing `mountMantineUi()` is invoked before `auditApp("app:init")`. Final project/reference/runtime checks remain with their existing owners. The system returns the PlusCal completion `"initialized_runtime"`; no new session object/envelope. React commit timing is not claimed verified or made into a new synchronization protocol. |
+| Failure | Candidate validation and prerequisite failures propagate without continuing into rendering/ready/API/mount/audit. There is no invented rollback of a successful initialization, caught-and-converted failure, retry or partial-startup success result. |
+
+## Fixture correspondence, not execution
+
+Existing regression15 is extended, without new IDs. It exercises actual `initializeFastFigure()` with call-local owner mocks, asserts project/registry/FSM → guard → supplied-startup → ready → expose → mount → audit, checks returned completion, and asserts a prerequisite failure is preserved and stops downstream work. It also exercises the actual candidate initializer against an empty-slot candidate and actual prerequisite guard against a missing callable. All mocked bindings/listener function/ready property descriptor are restored in finally; the fixture checks the live project identity and Interface revision remain unchanged. Existing supplied-reference audit tests remain. These fixtures were authored and statically inspected, **not run**.
+
+## Independent tree review correction and remaining scope
+
+Independent reviewer `0e250b82-85e9-4231-9c64-80c2c9c88a8b` blocked the original review004 documentation: trash confirmation and CSV metadata do not require new upstream meaning. Canonical traversal and the specified explicit-path `assets.readDeletionTarget` public route provide detached targets, rows/headerLines, owners and disjoint real-reference counts. The selected-only JS wrapper is an untranslated restriction, not lack of authority. Corrections are recorded atop review004 and explanation004; original patch004 is preserved, and patch005 records the correction rather than rewriting a historical diff. All-chart/slot display facts, especially editability of conversion/zero-reference charts, remain a genuine unavailable-public-read correspondence. No new tree envelope/API or Frontend Backend access is selected here, and no tree runtime migration is claimed.
+
